1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,555
This is Release Evidence Desk,
an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

2
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:09,739
Everything here is synthetic. Nothing connects
to Salesforce, and nothing is deployed.

3
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:13,732
I load the seed release,
and four fixed checks run in the browser.

4
00:00:14,042 --> 00:00:17,914
The AI-assisted Agentforce agent
passed its demo, but it's blocked.

5
00:00:17,974 --> 00:00:22,350
It needs an Apex class and a field that aren't
in the slice, or in the target org.

6
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:27,671
Every finding opens its evidence.
The graph shows both missing pieces in red.

7
00:00:27,982 --> 00:00:33,332
It also grants Modify All on Case, which bypasses
sharing. That's a protected blocker.

8
00:00:33,642 --> 00:00:41,092
Revision two is a pre-written fix. It adds the missing pieces,
narrows access to Read, and adds refusal and permission tests.

9
00:00:41,152 --> 00:00:44,755
The blockers clear.
Two access increases still need a human.

10
00:00:45,063 --> 00:00:49,482
I sign each one off with a name and a reason.
Both go into the memo.

11
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:53,346
Short reasons are refused,
and blockers can't be signed off at all.

12
00:00:53,406 --> 00:00:58,020
Each sign-off belongs to this revision only,
so it never carries over to a later one.

13
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:00,333
The slice is now ready to promote.

14
00:01:00,642 --> 00:01:04,060
Compare puts revision one beside revision two,
gate by gate.

15
00:01:04,369 --> 00:01:11,258
Now a blocked exception. This human-authored slice
deletes a field holding 3,412 records.

16
00:01:11,318 --> 00:01:14,717
That change is held back,
while the other three can still ship.

17
00:01:15,027 --> 00:01:20,372
Finally, I export the decision memo: what ships,
what's held, and who accepted which risk.

18
00:01:20,681 --> 00:01:25,426
It records a review decision, with evidence.
It never runs a deployment.
